KDE Connect over a VPN (branch remote-connect, upstream MR pending),
backported to kdeconnect-kde 26.04.3:
- custom devices may be IPv4 addresses or host names (e.g. Tailscale
  MagicDNS), resolved on every send; invalid entries are rejected when the
  list is set;
- while custom devices are set and a paired device is unreachable, the
  discovery packet is sent to them again, with backoff; right away when a
  LAN link drops; never to an address a LAN link is connected to;
- TCP_USER_TIMEOUT 60 s on LAN sockets (Linux);
- settings section "Devices by Address" in the KDE Connect app;
- no mDNS in LanLinkProvider's test mode (for its tests).

Generated with: git diff <last geolocation commit> stable-26.04.3.
Applies with -p1 after kdeconnect-26.04.3-geolocation-plugin.patch.

